#!/bin/sh
#
# HH71VM network-interface layout.
#
# eth0 - LAN: switch ports 0-3 plus CPU port 8 (mask 0x10f, VLAN 9). The only one
#        physical RJ45 sits on port 0, via external gigabit PHY (see.
#        /etc/init.d/rtl8197f-gphy).
# eth1 — port 4 of the switch (mask 0x110, VLAN 8). NOT externally displayed on this device;
#        left to exist so as not to diverge from the vendor table vlanconfig,
#        but has no role.
# eth2 - WAN: internal link to the Qualcomm side (modem) via USB/RNDIS.
#
# WHY eth2 AND NOT usb0. The name is given by usbnet: in usbnet_probe() the interface is called "usb%d"
# only for two host links, and for FLAG_ETHER (rndis_host has it) and locally
# unadministered MAC - "eth%d". The modem has MAC 00:26:23:3c:f1:37, the 0x02 bit is not set,
# therefore the 4.14 kernel gives exactly the eth name. Observed live: `rndis_host 1-1:1.0 eth2`.
# The number 2 is stable: eth0 and eth1 register the switch driver at an early boot stage,
# There are no other eth devices in the system. The stock showed usb0 - it has a different core, come to us
# it doesn't transfer. An alternative is renaming using the hotplug.d/net rule; we don't do
# an extra moving part for the sake of name cosmetics.
#
# WHY IS WAN HERE. HH71VM has two independent systems: Realtek (this one) and
# Qualcomm-modem. Only the second one goes outside, on the Internet, and they are connected internally.
# USB-link, where Realtek is the USB-host, and the modem is the RNDIS-device.
#
# ADDRESS ON WAN IS STATIC, NOT DHCP. Analysis of stock `/jffs2/bin/oem_start.sh`
# (2026-08-17) showed that the drain does not raise the DHCP client to usb0, but registers the address
# hands:
#     ifconfig usb0 192.168.225.111
#     route add default gw 192.168.225.1
#     dnrd --cache=off -s 192.168.225.1
# That is, there is apparently no DHCP server on the modem side at all, and the previous
# configuration `proto dhcp` would not receive an address even if the device appeared on
# tire. We repeat the flow literally: the same address, the same gateway, aka DNS.
# NAT is taken from the standard firewall zone wan.
#
# ⚠️ GATEWAY AND DNS DO NOT WORK HERE, they are exhibited in etc/uci-defaults/99-hh71vm-wan-gateway.
# Reason: /etc/config/network generates the /bin/config_generate script from board.json, and it
# takes exactly five fields from there - `ifname macaddr protocol ipaddr netmask`. All
# the rest is lost in silence. They are still transmitted below: they get into board.json and serve
# documentation, plus they will earn money themselves if this list is ever expanded.
#
# An early configuration used eth1 here before USB support was enabled:
# the role of WAN formally existed, but it led to nowhere.
#
# Switch port masks are set by the driver itself (rtl_nic.c), here there is only a role layout.

. /lib/functions/uci-defaults.sh

board_config_update
ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "eth0" "eth2"
ucidef_set_interface "wan" ifname "eth2" protocol "static" ipaddr "192.168.225.111" netmask "255.255.255.0" gateway "192.168.225.1" dns "192.168.225.1"
board_config_flush

exit 0
